---

<ArticleLayout
    title={title}
    description={description}
    author={author}
    authorUrl={authorUrl}
    pubDate={pubDate}
    readingTime={readingTime}
    image={image}
    imageAlt={imageAlt}
    category="VPN"
    categorySlug="vpn"
    headings={headings}
>
  <!-- Introduction -->
  <h2 id="introduction">Why Businesses Need Dedicated VPN Solutions</h2>
  <p>
    When your team worked from a single office, the corporate network handled security. Firewalls, access controls,
    and network monitoring protected everything inside the perimeter. Remote work changed that equation entirely.
  </p>
  <p>
    Now your employees connect from home networks, coffee shops, airports, and coworking spaces around the world.
    Each connection is a potential vulnerability. Client data, proprietary code, and internal communications travel
    across networks you don't control.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>A business VPN extends your security perimeter to wherever your team works.</strong> But business VPNs
    differ significantly from consumer solutions—they include centralized management, compliance features, and
    granular access controls that organizations require.
  </p>
  <p>
    We evaluated the leading business VPN solutions across deployment complexity, security features, pricing, and
    real-world usability. Here's what we found.
  </p>

  <!-- Business vs Consumer VPNs -->
  <h2 id="business-vs-consumer">Business VPN vs Consumer VPN: Key Differences</h2>
  <p>
    Consumer VPNs (like NordVPN or ExpressVPN) protect individual users. Business VPNs protect organizations.
    Here's how they differ:
  </p>

  <h3>Management & Control</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consumer:</strong> Each user manages their own account and settings</li>
    <li><strong>Business:</strong> Admin dashboard controls all users, permissions, and policies centrally</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Access Control</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consumer:</strong> Protects traffic but can't limit what users access</li>
    <li><strong>Business:</strong> Granular permissions—define who accesses which internal resources</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Identity Integration</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consumer:</strong> Separate credentials from company systems</li>
    <li><strong>Business:</strong> SSO integration with Google Workspace, Okta, Azure AD, etc.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Compliance & Auditing</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consumer:</strong> No logging (privacy feature)</li>
    <li><strong>Business:</strong> Detailed audit logs for compliance requirements</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Infrastructure</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consumer:</strong> Shared servers with other users</li>
    <li><strong>Business:</strong> Dedicated gateways and private servers for your organization</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>When to Choose Each</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Use a consumer VPN if:</strong> You're an individual freelancer or very small team (under 5) without
    compliance requirements or internal infrastructure to protect.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Use a business VPN if:</strong> You have internal resources to protect, need audit logs, must meet
    compliance standards, or want centralized control over team security.
  </p>

  <!-- Quick Comparison -->
  <h2 id="quick-comparison">Business VPN Quick Comparison</h2>
  <p>
    Here's how the top solutions compare on key criteria:
  </p>
  <ComparisonTable
      columns={quickCompareColumns}
      rows={quickCompareRows}
      caption="Business VPN solutions at a glance"
  />

  <!-- Top Business VPN Solutions -->
  <h2 id="top-solutions">Top 7 Business VPN Solutions</h2>

  <!-- NordLayer -->
  <h3 id="nordlayer">1. NordLayer — Best Overall for SMBs</h3>
  <p>
    NordLayer (formerly NordVPN Teams) combines enterprise-grade security with easy setup. It's the best choice
    for small to mid-size businesses that want powerful features without enterprise complexity.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes NordLayer stand out:</strong> The balance between sophistication and simplicity. You get
    zero-trust architecture, SSO integration, and comprehensive audit logs—but setup takes hours, not weeks.
    IT teams can deploy to 100 users in an afternoon.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key features:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Zero-trust network access:</strong> Verify every user and device before granting access</li>
    <li><strong>Centralized dashboard:</strong> Manage all users, permissions, and gateways in one place</li>
    <li><strong>SSO integration:</strong> Google Workspace, Okta, Azure AD, OneLogin, and more</li>
    <li><strong>Dedicated servers:</strong> Your traffic doesn't mix with other organizations</li>
    <li><strong>Smart Remote Access:</strong> Auto-connect when accessing specific resources</li>
    <li><strong>Device posture checks:</strong> Verify device security before granting access</li>
    <li><strong>SOC 2 Type 2 certified:</strong> Compliance-ready from day one</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Ideal for:</strong> Growing startups, small businesses, and mid-size companies (5-500 employees)
    who need enterprise security without enterprise complexity.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> $8/user/month (billed annually) for Core plan. Advanced and custom enterprise
    tiers available. 14-day free trial.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/nordlayer"
      text="Try NordLayer Free — 14-Day Trial"
      variant="primary"
      program="nordlayer"
  />

  <!-- Perimeter 81 -->
  <h3 id="perimeter-81">2. Perimeter 81 — Best for Mid-Size Enterprises</h3>
  <p>
    Perimeter 81 pioneered the software-defined perimeter approach and remains a leader in zero-trust network
    security. It's particularly strong for organizations with complex infrastructure needs.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes Perimeter 81 stand out:</strong> Deep infrastructure capabilities. You can segment
    networks, create micro-perimeters around sensitive resources, and integrate with existing security tools.
    The platform scales gracefully from 50 to 5,000+ users.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key features:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Software-defined perimeter:</strong> Create invisible networks around your resources</li>
    <li><strong>Network segmentation:</strong> Isolate departments, projects, or sensitivity levels</li>
    <li><strong>Multi-cloud support:</strong> Secure AWS, Azure, GCP, and on-premises together</li>
    <li><strong>DNS filtering:</strong> Block malicious domains at the network level</li>
    <li><strong>SIEM integration:</strong> Feed logs to Splunk, Datadog, or your existing tools</li>
    <li><strong>Site-to-site VPN:</strong> Connect office locations and cloud environments</li>
    <li><strong>HIPAA & PCI compliant:</strong> Purpose-built for regulated industries</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Ideal for:</strong> Mid-size enterprises (100-1000+ employees) with hybrid infrastructure,
    compliance requirements, or complex network architectures.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> $8/user/month (Essentials), $12/user/month (Premium), custom Enterprise pricing.
    Annual billing required. Free demo available.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/perimeter81"
      text="Get Perimeter 81 Demo"
      variant="primary"
      program="perimeter81"
  />

  <!-- Cisco AnyConnect -->
  <h3 id="cisco-anyconnect">3. Cisco AnyConnect — Best for Large Corporations</h3>
  <p>
    Cisco AnyConnect is the enterprise standard, trusted by Fortune 500 companies and government agencies.
    It's not the simplest solution, but for large organizations with existing Cisco infrastructure, it's
    often the natural choice.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes Cisco AnyConnect stand out:</strong> Deep integration with Cisco's security ecosystem—
    firewalls, identity services, and endpoint protection all work together. If you're already a Cisco shop,
    AnyConnect extends your existing investments.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key features:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Enterprise-grade reliability:</strong> Battle-tested at massive scale</li>
    <li><strong>Duo integration:</strong> Best-in-class MFA through Cisco's Duo platform</li>
    <li><strong>Network visibility:</strong> Deep analytics on user and traffic patterns</li>
    <li><strong>Umbrella integration:</strong> DNS-layer security included</li>
    <li><strong>Posture assessment:</strong> Detailed device compliance checking</li>
    <li><strong>Global support:</strong> 24/7 enterprise support with SLAs</li>
    <li><strong>On-premises option:</strong> Full control over your VPN infrastructure</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Ideal for:</strong> Large enterprises (500+ employees), government agencies, and organizations
    with existing Cisco infrastructure investments.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> Contact Cisco or a certified partner. Pricing is typically per-user or
    per-device with tiered support levels. Significant volume discounts available.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/cisco-anyconnect"
      text="Contact Cisco for Pricing"
      variant="secondary"
      program="cisco"
  />

  <!-- OpenVPN -->
  <h3 id="openvpn">4. OpenVPN Access Server — Best Self-Hosted Solution</h3>
  <p>
    OpenVPN Access Server gives you complete control over your VPN infrastructure. Self-host on your own
    servers, cloud VMs, or containers—you own the data and the configuration.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes OpenVPN stand out:</strong> No third-party dependencies. Your VPN traffic never
    touches external servers. For organizations with strict data sovereignty requirements or existing
    infrastructure, this is the most flexible option.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key features:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Complete control:</strong> Deploy on any Linux server or cloud platform</li>
    <li><strong>No subscription fees:</strong> Free for up to 2 concurrent connections; one-time license fees for more
    </li>
    <li><strong>Open source transparency:</strong> Audit the code yourself</li>
    <li><strong>Web-based admin:</strong> Manage users and access through browser interface</li>
    <li><strong>LDAP/RADIUS/SAML:</strong> Integrate with existing identity systems</li>
    <li><strong>Custom configuration:</strong> Fine-tune every aspect of your VPN</li>
    <li><strong>Multi-cloud:</strong> Deploy gateways anywhere—AWS, Azure, GCP, on-premises</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Ideal for:</strong> Organizations with DevOps/IT staff, strict compliance requirements,
    or existing infrastructure where third-party managed services aren't acceptable.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> Free for 2 concurrent connections. $15/concurrent connection for additional
    capacity (one-time license). Your hosting/infrastructure costs on top.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/openvpn"
      text="Get OpenVPN Access Server"
      variant="secondary"
      program="openvpn"
  />

  <!-- Twingate -->
  <h3 id="twingate">5. Twingate — Best Zero-Trust Architecture</h3>
  <p>
    Twingate takes the zero-trust model to its logical conclusion—replacing traditional VPNs entirely with
    software-defined access controls. There's no VPN client collecting all traffic; instead, access is
    granted per-resource with continuous verification.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes Twingate stand out:</strong> The architecture is fundamentally different. Rather than
    routing all traffic through a VPN tunnel, Twingate creates direct, encrypted connections to specific
    resources. This means better performance and tighter security—users only access what they need, when they need it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key features:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Zero-trust by design:</strong> No network-level access, only resource-level</li>
    <li><strong>Invisible to users:</strong> Works in the background with no manual connections</li>
    <li><strong>Split tunneling built-in:</strong> Only work traffic goes through Twingate</li>
    <li><strong>Resource-based permissions:</strong> Grant access to specific apps, not entire networks</li>
    <li><strong>Device trust:</strong> Verify device security posture before each connection</li>
    <li><strong>No public IP exposure:</strong> Internal resources aren't internet-accessible</li>
    <li><strong>Generous free tier:</strong> Up to 5 users free forever</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Ideal for:</strong> Tech-forward companies, startups prioritizing security architecture, and
    organizations replacing legacy VPNs with modern zero-trust approaches.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> Free for up to 5 users. $5/user/month (Starter), $10/user/month (Business),
    custom Enterprise pricing. No minimum user counts.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/twingate"
      text="Try Twingate Free — Up to 5 Users"
      variant="primary"
      program="twingate"
  />

  <!-- GoodAccess -->
  <h3 id="goodaccess">6. GoodAccess — Best for Growing Startups</h3>
  <p>
    GoodAccess offers enterprise features at startup-friendly prices. It's particularly popular with EU-based
    companies due to strong GDPR compliance and European data center options.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes GoodAccess stand out:</strong> The value proposition. You get dedicated gateways,
    zero-trust features, and comprehensive management for less than most competitors. Startup discounts
    make it even more accessible for early-stage companies.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key features:</strong>
  </p>
