  <!-- Implementation Guide -->
  <h2 id="implementation-guide">Implementation Guide</h2>
  <p>
    Here's a practical roadmap for deploying a business VPN:
  </p>

  <h3>Phase 1: Planning (1-2 Weeks)</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Inventory resources:</strong> List everything that needs protection—internal tools, databases, staging
      environments, cloud resources
    </li>
    <li><strong>Map access patterns:</strong> Who needs access to what? Document current permissions</li>
    <li><strong>Identify compliance needs:</strong> SOC 2, HIPAA, GDPR, PCI—what applies to you?</li>
    <li><strong>Evaluate solutions:</strong> Trial 2-3 options with a small pilot group</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Phase 2: Setup (1-2 Days for Cloud Solutions)</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Configure identity:</strong> Connect SSO provider (Google Workspace, Okta, Azure AD)</li>
    <li><strong>Deploy gateways:</strong> Set up connections to your cloud/internal resources</li>
    <li><strong>Define access policies:</strong> Create permission groups based on roles</li>
    <li><strong>Test with admins:</strong> Verify functionality before broader rollout</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Phase 3: Rollout (1-2 Weeks)</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Communicate to team:</strong> Explain why you're implementing a VPN and how it affects them</li>
    <li><strong>Staged deployment:</strong> Start with tech-savvy users, then expand</li>
    <li><strong>Provide documentation:</strong> Create guides for common tasks</li>
    <li><strong>Support channel:</strong> Establish how users get help with issues</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Phase 4: Ongoing Management</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Regular access reviews:</strong> Quarterly audit of who has access to what</li>
    <li><strong>Log monitoring:</strong> Watch for unusual access patterns</li>
    <li><strong>User onboarding:</strong> Include VPN setup in new hire process</li>
    <li><strong>Offboarding:</strong> Revoke access immediately when employees leave</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- Security Compliance -->
  <h2 id="compliance">Security Compliance Considerations</h2>
  <p>
    Business VPNs often need to meet specific compliance frameworks. Here's what to verify:
  </p>

  <h3>SOC 2 Type 2</h3>
  <p>
    Most business VPNs now have SOC 2 certification. Request the report and verify it covers the services
    you'll use. NordLayer, Perimeter 81, Twingate, and Cloudflare are all SOC 2 certified.
  </p>

  <h3>HIPAA (Healthcare)</h3>
  <p>
    If you handle Protected Health Information (PHI), you need a Business Associate Agreement (BAA).
    NordLayer, Perimeter 81, and Cisco offer HIPAA-compliant configurations with BAAs.
  </p>

  <h3>GDPR (EU Data)</h3>
  <p>
    All major business VPNs support GDPR compliance. Key considerations: where data is processed,
    whether you can limit data to EU regions, and Data Processing Agreements (DPAs).
  </p>

  <h3>PCI DSS (Payment Data)</h3>
  <p>
    If you process payment card data, your VPN should support PCI DSS requirements. Perimeter 81 and
    Cisco specifically address PCI compliance in their documentation.
  </p>

